ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+02:44/60:00 c13/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_miyoqghu","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/census-window.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[10:00:53] == census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-16 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\n--- aggregate: runs=0 timeouts=0 exit1=0\n--- requests in window: 0 (log rotated past window or clean window)\nVERDICT: clean window, H1 supported\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-17 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\nno journald lines for continuo in window (clean or unit not logging)\n\n[census-update] continuo census-window output for 2026-09-17:\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-17 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\n | to= | turns=0, tools=46, exit=0 \nSep 17 00:10:38 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=33, exit=0 \nSep 17 00:40:39 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=49, exit=0 \n--- aggregate: runs=3 timeouts=0 exit1=0\n--- requests in window: n=354 latency: median=8s max=338s over60s=10\nVERDICT: clean window -- H1 supported (workload converted to fast closes)\n\n[t+03:18/60:00 c14